// The Faktor Native Protocol v1 client (docs/native-protocol.md): a typed
// java.net.http client of the daemon's OWN surface. The frozen v7.5.6 wire
// surface in BackendProcessManager stays untouched migration glue; this
// client is what the real frontend renders from.
//
// Rules observed:
//  - auth is the ephemeral password generated by BackendProcessManager and
//    handed to the child through the environment (protected channel, never
//    argv or disk): `Authorization: Bearer <password>`.
//  - every response body is read through a streaming byte cap; oversized
//    bodies are closed and rejected, never buffered unbounded.
//  - every request carries a timeout; non-2xx bodies are mapped to
//    NativeApiException with the daemon's `{error:{code,message,retryable}}`.
//  - shapes are parsed by dev.faktor.shared native parsers, so drift is a
//    loud NativeProtocolException, never a silently wrong UI.
